// spec: 12 Runtime panics; 4 Types as values
// panics: type-expr
// A panic while a type expression resolves forgets every declaration the expression began, so
// the next expression that reaches one of them starts over and fails the same way, instead of
// finding a half-built declaration left behind; the checker rejects the program, since the body
// of B names a value.
var bad = 1
type A = { c: C, b: B }
type C = { a: A }
type B = Array[bad]
println(Panic.catch({ type(A) }) is Err)
println("again")
println(type(C))

// expect
// out: true
// out: again
// exit: 1
// err: bad is not a type
